Sval: Linux names that are Sval's own, apart from an installed Firefox's

Firefox and Sval run side by side without touching each other's state.
Four Linux names in Gecko are Firefox's whatever the application's
identity:

- The crash helper writes its log before Gecko gives it the data
  directory, and guessed it as ~/.mozilla/firefox or
  ~/.config/mozilla/firefox, so it truncated Firefox's
  crash_helper_server.log. With a profile name it takes the directory
  Gecko gives that build, ~/.sval. The mozbuild crate carries
  MOZ_APP_PROFILE for it.
- The MPRIS bus name started org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.firefox, so media
  keys, playerctl -p firefox and desktop rules aimed at Firefox also
  drove Sval.
- The Wayland picture-in-picture window took the app id
  org.mozilla.firefox, so the compositor grouped it with Firefox. It takes
  the program name, which is the app id of Sval's other windows.
- The GNOME search provider's result icon named Firefox's icon.

diff --git a/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp b/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp
index 2c3157f..e021a5a 100644
--- a/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp
+++ b/browser/components/shell/nsGNOMEShellDBusHelper.cpp
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@ static already_AddRefed<GVariant> DBusAppendSearchID(const char* aID) {
                           g_variant_new_string(gnomeSearchTitle.get()));
     // TODO: When running on flatpak/snap we may need to use
     // icon like org.mozilla.Firefox or so.
-    g_variant_builder_add(&b, "{sv}", "gicon", g_variant_new_string("firefox"));
+    g_variant_builder_add(&b, "{sv}", "gicon", g_variant_new_string("sval"));
   }
 
   return dont_AddRef(g_variant_ref_sink(g_variant_builder_end(&b)));
